#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1364 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "any-branch 2: an 'ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED' subject has an empty ACTARMCD but a populated ACTARM -> fires on row 1. RE-PINNED by M2-D25 (exact, case-sensitive CT comparison): the rows carried 'Assigned, Not Treated' in mixed case while the Check normalised with upper(); with upper() retired the data now carries the exact ARMNULRS submission value, preserving the any-branch-2 coverage. Pin addresses by identity (USUBJID) since #expectViolationAt values must be space-free."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ACTARMCD type=Char label="Actual Arm Code"
col ACTARM   type=Char label="Description of Actual Arm"
col ARMNRS   type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 |  | Arm A | ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |  |       | ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED
